course: dictionary
lesson: 1923
title: Comfort: one word, many shades
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Comfort is a word with more than one meaning. It can be a feeling, a thing that helps, or something you do for someone. The words around it, the context, tell you which meaning to pick.
explain: «Jess gave her little brother a hug and tried to comfort him.» Here comfort is a doing word. To comfort someone means to make them feel less sad or scared.
explain: «The warm bed was pure comfort after the cold, wet walk.» Here comfort is a thing you feel: a warm, relaxed, pleasant feeling. Check it by swapping in a meaning: "The warm bed was pure relaxed, pleasant feeling" makes sense, so you have the right one.
fact: Comfort can be a noun (a thing or feeling) or a verb (a doing word): «comfort» and «comforts» are both used.
fact: «Comfort» as a verb means to make someone feel less sad or scared.
fact: «Comforts» in the plural means things that make life easy and pleasant, like a warm bed or a soft chair.
fact: «Take comfort in» means to find help or hope in something, as in «Christians find comfort in Psalm 23».
fact: Phrases: «too close for comfort» means so near that it makes you feel uneasy, and «comfort food» is food that makes you feel good.
exercise: In «Friends visit with food and comfort», what does comfort mean? | Being in a hurry | *Kind help that makes people feel less sad | A hard, cold thing
exercise: «The warm bed gave Sam comfort after the cold, wet day.» What does comfort mean here? | To make someone less sad | A kind of cold drink | *A pleasant feeling of warmth and rest
exercise: Find the doing word (verb) in this sentence: «Mum tried to comfort the baby.» | the | baby | *comfort | Mum
test:
«It was too close for comfort when the car stopped inches from the kerb.» What does too close for comfort mean? | So near that it makes you feel uneasy | *So near that it makes you feel uneasy, but in a good way, like a hug | Far away and safe | Very quiet and calm
test:
«Lily found comfort in her favourite old book.» What does comfort mean here? | *Help and hope that made her feel better | To make someone less sad | A type of book | A fast, noisy game
exam:
In America, what does «comfort station» mean, as in a park? | A shop that sells blankets | *A public toilet | A quiet place to sit and read | A kind of bench
